From: Andy <andylee77@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 12:50:44 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 04/13] infinity6c: build against the upstream HAL interface

John's backend uses interface items only his fork's raptor_hal.h has. When
RSS_ISP_AUTO is absent (upstream), i6c_upstream_compat.h selects
I6C_UPSTREAM_HAL_IFACE and the backend adapts:
- defines RSS_ISP_AUTO and rss_isp_knob_t;
- wraps the six int* ISP getters as upstream's uint8_t* ones;
- drops the knob-caps op and the green WB gain;
- forces the sensor mode to auto;
- guards .max_enc_pixel_rate.
+70/-6, all inside the backend.
---
